 "title": "Decoding Common Interview Questions",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This video breaks down what interviewers actually want to hear when they ask standard interview questions. It helps candidates understand the underlying intent behind common questions like strengths, weaknesses, and background.",
 "key_points": [
  "Where do you see yourself in 5 years? -> Interviewers want to hear: How long do you plan to stay with the company?",
  "Why do you want to join us? -> Interviewers want to hear: How much research have you done on the company?",
  "What are your strengths? -> Interviewers want to hear: What do you bring to the table?",
  "What are your weaknesses? -> Interviewers want to hear: How self-aware are you and what have you done to improve on those weaknesses?",
  "Do you have any questions for me? -> Interviewers want to hear: Your ability to make conversation and curiosity.",
  "Tell me about yourself? -> Interviewers want to hear: Can you name something that's not in the resume? That's also very interesting about you?",
  "What do you do outside of work? -> Interviewers want to hear: Do you have any hobbies or passions that you kept over a long period of time?"
 ],
